# Every image a benchmark box needs to pull from a public registry, fully
# qualified with its upstream host so scripts/benchmark/registry_mirror.sh
# and seed_image_cache.sh can route each one to the right proxy/registry
# without guessing (NOFireAI/sregym#150). One per line, "<host>/<path>:<tag>".
# Blank lines and "#" comments are ignored.
#
# Covers sregym-lite only: the images below are what lite's current 21
# problems pull. A problem outside lite is not covered here; see
# NOFireAI/sregym#152 for extending this list to every problem set and
# #153 for a periodic check that these pinned tags still match what each
# chart or manifest resolves to upstream.
#
# Adding an image is one line here, then `scripts/benchmark/seed_image_cache.sh`.
# Re-seed whenever this file gains a line or an existing tag changes meaning
# (a ":latest"-style tag that moved upstream). See NOFIRE.md's registry
# mirror section for the full seeding/re-seeding story.
#
# How this list was built: `helm template` of every app's own Helm chart
# (sregym/service/metadata/*.json's chart_path, the same derivation the old
# per-attempt pre-pull step used to do at deploy time, now run once here
# instead of once per attempt), the raw manifests for the two apps
# that skip Helm (hotel-reservation, blueprint-hotel-reservation,
# helm_deploy=False), the always-on telemetry stack's charts (prometheus,
# loki, promtail) and raw manifests (jaeger, otel-collector, khaos), the
# wrk2 load generator's own job template, the custom-service fault's two
# hand-built images, the edge agent's pinned release, and a grep of every
# fault injector and problem file for an image literal with a real (not
# "app-image:latest"-style fake) tag. Not derived by a script, so a missed
# image is plausible; the seed script's own verification pass (`crane
# validate --remote` against a fresh registry pointed at the same bucket) is
# what catches one before it reaches a benchmark run. tests/benchmark/
# test_image_cache_completeness.py is a second, independent check: it scans
# sregym/ and kind/ for image literals and fails if one is missing from this
# list, so a new fault or chart file cannot drift this list silently. That
# scan verifies the lite problem set fully (every lite image literal lives
# under sregym/ or kind/, nothing in the SREGym-applications submodule). The
# non-lite TidbCluster images below (pingcap/pd, pingcap/tikv, pingcap/tidb,
# the busybox helper default) are verified only by a static read of the
# operator's own defaulting source and the submodule's CR, not by this scan:
# they are rendered from SREGym-applications/FleetCast/tidb-operator/
# tidb-cluster.yaml, outside both SCAN_DIRS and this list's own "known,
# deliberate gaps" reasoning below, so a future change to that CR or that
# operator version will not be caught here automatically.
#
# metrics-server, the OpenEBS operator, Calico, and the tidb-operator CRDs
# and fault-recovery CR used to be fetched from their upstream URLs at
# deploy time; they are now vendored under sregym/resources/vendored/ and
# kind/manifests/ (see that directory's README for source URL, version, and
# refresh steps) and applied from the local file instead. Because those
# vendored files live under sregym/ and kind/, the completeness scan above
# covers their "image:" keys and env "value:" fields the same as any other
# raw manifest in this tree; nothing extra to maintain here for them.
#
# registry:2 and the kind node image (jacksonarthurclark/aiopslab-kind-x86)
# are cached too, under scripts/benchmark/seed_host_images.sh's
# "host-images/" prefix in the same bucket, not as lines in this list: the
# HOST pulls both directly (`docker run registry:2`, `kind create cluster`),
# never through the in-cluster containerd this list's mirror covers, so
# neither one is a "<host>/<path>:<tag>" line registry_mirror.sh could route.
# See that script's header for the caching mechanism.
#
# Known, deliberate gaps, not in this list and not mirrored:
#   - train-ticket's own per-microservice images. Its chart's job
#     (ghcr.io/sregym/train-ticket-deploy, listed below) applies the rest of
#     train-ticket's manifests itself at install time, so `helm template`
#     never renders their `image:` fields. That job's own image is cached;
#     what it pulls when it runs is not.
#   - ghcr.io/sregym/sregym-mcp:latest. The benchmark never pulls it:
#     build_mcp_image.sh builds this repo's MCP server locally and
#     `kind load`s it with imagePullPolicy: Never (see NOFIRE.md).
#   - Anything astronomy-shop's own extra_args disable at real deploy time
#     (the chart's bundled quay.io/prometheus/prometheus:v3.9.0, the
#     flagd-ui sidecar). Harmless to cache anyway, so left in rather than
#     hand-pruned; a chart version bump will not silently break seeding over
#     an image that was never going to be pulled.
#   - Every chart or manifest still fetched from a remote helm repo or a raw
#     GitHub URL at deploy time, for an app no sregym-lite problem deploys
#     today (noise=false, M2 never reaches it): ingress-nginx, chaos-mesh,
#     the pingcap Helm repo's own `pingcap/tidb-operator` chart coordinates
#     (the CRDs and recovery CR it applies ARE vendored; the chart itself is
#     still a live `helm repo add`), the fleetcast and flight-ticket chart
#     repos, and the TidbCluster CR's own `config_url`. With kind's
#     containerd `_default` host mirror fail-closed (NOFIRE.md's registry
#     mirror section), enabling noise or running a problem that deploys one
#     of these apps fails closed (ImagePullBackOff, or a `helm repo add`
#     network error upstream of any image pull) rather than silently
#     reaching the internet. Out of scope here; NOFireAI/sregym#152 covers
#     extending this vendoring and caching to every problem set, not just
#     lite.

# --- docker.io ---------------------------------------------------------
docker.io/library/busybox:1.36
# init_container_dependency_hang's dep-wait init container pins this exact
# tag: a newer busybox regressed the nslookup exit code this fault's wait
# loop depends on (kubernetes/website#12050).
docker.io/library/busybox:1.28
docker.io/library/busybox:latest
# tidb-operator's default helper image (pd/tikv/tidb's init container) when
# a TidbCluster CR sets no helper.image of its own, which
# SREGym-applications/FleetCast/tidb-operator/tidb-cluster.yaml does not:
# confirmed from tidb-operator v1.6.0's own source
# (pkg/apis/pingcap/v1alpha1/tidbcluster.go's defaultHelperImage). This is a
# different CR from inject_operator.py's fault-recovery CR below, which does
# set helper.image explicitly (to alpine:3.16.0).
docker.io/library/busybox:1.26.2
docker.io/library/redis:6.2.4
docker.io/library/memcached:1.6.7
docker.io/library/memcached:1.6.39-alpine
docker.io/library/memcached:latest
docker.io/library/mongo:4.4.6
docker.io/library/mongo:8.0.14-rc0
docker.io/library/mongo:latest
docker.io/library/postgres:17.6
docker.io/library/python:3.9-slim
docker.io/library/python:3.10-slim
docker.io/library/python:3.12-alpine
docker.io/library/python:3.12-slim
docker.io/library/ubuntu:22.04
